---
import type {Report} from '../lib/models';
import {date} from '../lib/config';
import Icon from './Icon.astro';
interface Props {report:Report;sample?:boolean;input?:string;}
const {report,sample=false,input}=Astro.props;
const statuses={record:'Record found','no-match':'No matching record found',unavailable:'Coverage unavailable'};
---
<div class="report-header"><div><span class="eyebrow">{sample?'SYNTHETIC SAMPLE REPORT':'YOUR REPORT IS READY'}</span><h1>{report.identity.year} {report.identity.make}<br/>{report.identity.model}</h1><p class="small">VIN: {report.identity.vin||'Not verified — synthetic demo vehicle'}</p><p>{report.identity.body} · {report.identity.engine}</p>{input&&<p class="identifier">Submitted identifier: {input}</p>}</div><span class="report-stamp"><Icon name="file" size={42}/> DEMO REPORT</span></div><div class="report-meta"><span>Report generated: {date(report.generatedAt)}</span><span>Fixture source freshness: {date(report.sourceFreshness)}</span></div><div class="finding"><Icon name="alert" size={28}/><div><span class="mini-label">START HERE</span><h2>A damage entry deserves a closer look.</h2><p>This synthetic report includes front-end damage. Ask the seller for repair invoices, details of the impact, and an independent inspection. Severity and repair quality are unknown.</p><a href="#event-damage">View supporting entry ↗</a></div></div><h2>Coverage at a glance</h2><div class="coverage-grid">{report.coverage.map(c=><article><span class="status-tag">{statuses[c.status]}</span><h3>{c.category}</h3><p>{c.note}</p></article>)}</div><div class="report-detail"><section><span class="eyebrow">THE DOCUMENTED STORY</span><h2>Vehicle timeline</h2><ol class="timeline">{report.events.map(event=><li id={`event-${event.id}`}><time>{event.date}</time><h3>{event.title}</h3>{event.mileage!==undefined&&<strong>{event.mileage.toLocaleString('en-US')} miles</strong>}<p>{event.detail}</p><span class="small">Source: {event.source}</span></li>)}</ol></section><section class="mileage-panel"><span class="eyebrow">MILEAGE SNAPSHOT</span><h2>62,480 <span class="small">mi</span></h2><p>Latest recorded reading · Sep 2026</p><svg viewBox="0 0 330 180" width="330" height="180" role="img" aria-label="Synthetic mileage rises from 18 miles in 2019 to 28,140 in 2022 and 62,480 in 2026."><g stroke="#1F1F1E" opacity=".15"><path d="M30 20h280M30 65h280M30 110h280M30 155h280"/></g><path d="M35 154L155 93L299 25" stroke="#1F1F1E" stroke-width="3" fill="none"/><g fill="#FE5701" stroke="#1F1F1E" stroke-width="2"><circle cx="35" cy="154" r="5"/><circle cx="155" cy="93" r="5"/><circle cx="299" cy="25" r="5"/></g><g font-size="12" fill="#1F1F1E"><text x="25" y="178">2019</text><text x="141" y="178">2022</text><text x="280" y="178">2026</text></g></svg><p class="small">Gaps between readings are unknown. A rising line does not rule out odometer changes.</p><h3>Take these questions with you</h3><ul><li>Can I see the repair invoices?</li><li>Does the odometer match recent records?</li><li>Can an independent mechanic inspect it?</li></ul><a href="/guides/buying-checklist/">Open the buyer checklist ↗</a></section></div><p class="notice">All entries on this page are synthetic examples, not facts about a real vehicle. No matching record does not mean an incident never occurred. Coverage varies by vehicle and provider.</p>
